":"1795274293143152001-746d1ab8-d3fa-4c59-8347-c19ecee3ea8a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"a0e68ee5cc5d948794547822f4581f2c3e582a25e8240bcc93bcaac959f58e4f","event_uuid":"cf5cf911-0319-42df-9463-f966df7219b3","position":{"commit_sha":"f021eb30f7b4e51f7466ceb23673c31cc1d47de7","position":"1795275071254236001-cf5cf911-0319-42df-9463-f966df7219b3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"181f11da7efc65fb6f22ac3578b0f24b925a0318742a0718278539438260881a","event_uuid":"6e3ff32f-25f5-4380-bc42-2fb7d260746e","position":{"commit_sha":"beaac48bce18fbca84e31f17811219b4cde02ff5","position":"1795275181339139001-6e3ff32f-25f5-4380-bc42-2fb7d260746e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"38c680ef5f1985608b8bb4002334d95f1c825772a10c50f56c5cf2beb70b28f6","event_uuid":"03f46e05-ae36-4f41-a39c-2fa33ded1761","position":{"commit_sha":"4632c28b2ed58866c649f560cb6ea08338ee6b35","position":"1795275206935208001-03f46e05-ae36-4f41-a39c-2fa33ded1761"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root-cause findings (2026-11-21 PST, rebar-session-05f74084). There are 6 sub-causes, 3 of them product defects. Evidence: Windows JUnit run 44681457334, Windows probe run 44900309390, and local macOS runs with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL setting core.autocrlf=true. Local result: 2 of the 11 fail and 8 pass; the rest need Windows text mode.\n1. PRODUCT: `rebar._store.gitutil.run_git` (and `_run_in_group`) passes str stdin with `text=True`. On Windows, Python's text-mode stdin rewrites every `\\n` as `\\r\\n`, so every caller that pipes text to git sends CRLF. Probe run 44900309390 shows the effect: `update-index --index-info` fed that way records NO entries (bytes stdin records all 3 stages). Test: test_run_git_wrapper::test_str_input_is_forwarded_to_stdin (piped hash != file hash).\n2. PRODUCT: `rebar.llm.evals.plan_replay.tier2` (tier2.py:225) writes `objects/info/alternates` with `open(..., \"w\")`. On Windows the line ends in `\\r\\n`, git keeps the `\\r` in the path (\"objects?\"), the objects are not found, and `git reset --hard` exits 128. Tests: the 4 test_plan_replay_tier2 materialize tests.\n3. PRODUCT (ops tooling): `infra/scripts/reclaim_bridge_history.py` main() refuses `scratch worktree is not clean` because `git status --porcelain` reports line-ending-only differences under core.autocrlf=true. This reproduces locally with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL autocrlf=true. Test: test_reclaim_bridge_history::test_unrelated_remote_ref_movement_does_not_fail_dry_run (the script exits 1 before its 2nd ls-remote, so the test's ref assertion fails).\n4. TEST HARNESS: `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.extract_store_snapshot` uses `git archive`, which applies core.autocrlf, so extracted event files come out CRLF. This reproduces locally. Test: test_dc_store_copy_bounded_25e0::test_the_bounded_slice_still_carries_real_tickets_and_store_metadata.\n5. CHECKOUT: the vendored, SHA-256-pinned files `tests/external/live_jira_dc/pycontribs-jira-LICENSE.txt` and `.github/schemas/gitlab-ci.schema.json` have no eol attribute, so a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows system default) converts them to CRLF and their pinned hashes no longer match. Tests: test_jira_dc_harness_shape, test_bridge_provider_wrappers, test_reconcile_workflow_lint.\n6. TEST: test_mcp_publisher_pin::_verify pipes `\"<sha>  <file>\\n\"` to `sha256sum -c` with text=True, and sha256sum sees `'mcp-publisher.tar.gz'$'\\r'`.\nNote: cause 1's mechanism (text-mode stdin) is also what breaks cold-censorable-armedcrab's unmerged-recovery fixture. That test helper is fixed under that ticket; the product run_git belongs here.","timestamp":1795261965856911001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction to finding 3 (reclaim_bridge_history). The macOS 'scratch worktree is not clean' reproduction is an artifact. The test passes an environment that replaces the whole env, so my GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL autocrlf config was dropped for the script's git while the worktree had been checked out CRLF; with the config visible, 'git status --porcelain' is clean (ls-files --eol shows i/lf w/crlf, porcelain ''). On Windows the cause is different and not line endings: the test injects the unrelated ref through a '#!/bin/sh' file named 'git' prepended to PATH. Windows CreateProcess never runs it (no .exe), so the ls-remote counter never fires, refs/heads/unrelated is never created, and the test's rev-parse exits 128. That is a POSIX-shell-stub defect (the posix-shell-stubs class, transhuman-wounded-pangolin's tests/_exe_stub.py helper), not CRLF. infra/scripts/reclaim_bridge_history.py has no line-ending defect on this evidence.","timestamp":1795272548169545001}],"created_at":1795154110807042001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7e61bfee-7b82-4cd4-9bb7-aa57779e2b9f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750"},{"link_uuid":"8f893a03-3f14-476c-9f38-029d9a0a60e8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a2da-e61b-989e-4862"},{"link_uuid":"ef2ff312-29d9-4abe-b3ca-df313a90be5a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"e062-1686-1a27-41a4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff. The 11 entries of `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args` belong to this bug. Root-cause evidence (Windows JUnit 44681457334, probe run 44900309390, local macOS runs under core.autocrlf=true) is in this ticket's comments. Depends on transhuman-wounded-pangolin for one test (sub-cause 6).\n\n## Root cause (6 sub-causes; 2 in product code)\n1. **Product contract: `gitutil.run_git` / `_run_in_group` pipe str stdin in text mode.** On Windows Python rewrites each `\\n` as `\\r\\n`, so git receives CRLF. `hash-object --stdin` then hashes different bytes. No shipped caller is affected today: `reconciler/_ref_lock.py` already hashes bytes with `text=False`, and `_snapshot/delta_tree.py`'s checkout-index payload is NUL-separated. The fix makes `run_git`'s documented str-stdin contract platform-stable. The same translation makes `update-index --index-info` record nothing (probe run 44900309390), though no product caller does that today. Test: `test_run_git_wrapper::test_str_input_is_forwarded_to_stdin`.\n2. **Product: `llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py` writes `objects/info/alternates` in text mode.** The `\\r` stays in the path, the borrowed objects are not found, and `git reset --hard` exits 128. Tests: the 4 `test_plan_replay_tier2` materialize tests.\n3. **Checkout: 2 SHA-256-pinned vendored files carry no eol attribute.** Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so they check out CRLF and their pins fail. The files are `tests/external/live_jira_dc/pycontribs-jira-LICENSE.txt` and `.github/schemas/gitlab-ci.schema.json`. Tests: `test_jira_dc_harness_shape`, `test_bridge_provider_wrappers`, `test_reconcile_workflow_lint`.\n4. **Test harness: `_dc_fixtures.extract_store_snapshot` uses `git archive`, which applies core.autocrlf**, so extracted events come out CRLF. Test: `test_dc_store_copy_bounded_25e0` (this one reproduces on macOS too).\n5. **Test: `test_mcp_publisher_pin._verify` pipes the checksum line in text mode**, so `sha256sum` sees `'mcp-publisher.tar.gz'$'\\r'`.\n6. **Test: `test_reclaim_bridge_history::test_unrelated_remote_ref_movement_does_not_fail_dry_run` injects its ref through a `#!/bin/sh` file named `git` on PATH.** Windows never runs it, so the ref is never created and `rev-parse` exits 128. This is not line endings; it is the shell-stub problem transhuman-wounded-pangolin solves with `tests/_exe_stub.py`.\n\n## Approach\n1. `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py`: when `text=True` and `input_data` is str:\n   - Encode it with `_GIT_ENCODING`/`_GIT_ERRORS` (the codec text mode used) and run in binary mode with `check=False`.\n   - Decode stdout/stderr with the same codec and subprocess's universal-newline translation (`\\r\\n`→`\\n`, `\\r`→`\\n`), so returned text is identical on POSIX.\n   - Only then apply `check`, raising `CalledProcessError` with the decoded str. A `TimeoutExpired` gets its `output`/`stderr` decoded the same way.\n   - Apply the same in `_run_in_group`.\n   - The bytes-input contract and its TypeError are unchanged.\n   - `tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py::test_str_input_is_forwarded_to_stdin` writes its comparison file with `write_text`, which also writes CRLF on Windows. It will write `content.encode()` with `write_bytes`, so both sides hash the same LF bytes.\n2. `tier2.py`: open the alternates file with `newline=\"\\n\"`.\n3. `.gitattributes`: mark the 2 vendored pinned files `-text` so no checkout converts them. Their blobs are LF today (`ls-files --eol` shows `i/lf`), so the bytes are unchanged.\n4. `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py`: run `git -c core.autocrlf=false archive`.\n5. `tests/unit/test_mcp_publisher_pin.py`: pipe the checksum line as bytes.\n6. `test_reclaim_bridge_history.py`, `test_unrelated_remote_ref_movement_does_not_fail_dry_run`:\n   - Build the ls-remote shim with pangolin's `tests/_exe_stub.py` (a Python-body stub that Windows can run) instead of a `#!/bin/sh` file.\n   - Build the child environment as `{**os.environ, \"PATH\": os.pathsep.join([str(wrapper_dir), str(Path(git_executable).parent), os.environ.get(\"PATH\", \"\")]), ...test vars}`, so the stub dir is a real first PATH entry on every OS and Windows keeps SYSTEMROOT/PATHEXT. Today the `:`-joined PATH replaces the whole environment.\n   - This waits for pangolin's change on main.\n- New regression tests:\n  - `tests/unit/test_run_git_stdin_bytes.py`:\n    - With `subprocess.run` spied, a str `input_data` reaches subprocess as encoded bytes with `text` false. The decoded stdout is unchanged (including `\\r\\n`→`\\n`), and a failing `check=True` call raises `CalledProcessError` carrying str.\n    - With `subprocess.Popen` spied, the same holds for `_run_in_group` (reached through `run_git(timeout=...)`).\n  - In `test_plan_replay_tier2`, an assertion that the alternates file contains no `\\r`.\n- No config key, env var or flag.\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args`: remove each line whose test passes in the Windows validation run. If the file ends up empty, delete it and its `@` line in `.github/workflows/test.yml`.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py\n- .gitattributes\n- tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py\n- tests/unit/test_mcp_publisher_pin.py\n- tests/integration/test_reclaim_bridge_history.py\n- tests/unit/test_run_git_stdin_bytes.py\n- tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py\n- tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py\n- .github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args\n- .github/workflows/test.yml (only if the args file is deleted)\n\n## Testing\n- Pre-merge Windows validation on the exact fixed tree, with the lines removed: push `tmp/b4-neglectful-acceptable-gerbil`, dispatch `gh workflow run 294845723 --ref tmp/b4-neglectful-acceptable-gerbil`, and record the run id in a comment. Then delete the tmp branch.\n- AC1 evidence: the first scheduled `test.yml` run on main whose head contains the merge commit. Its run id goes in a comment before the close.\n- `make verify` through verify-slot.sh.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `crlf.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `crlf.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":".gitattributes","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":"tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_publisher_pin.py","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_reclaim_bridge_history.py","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_run_git_stdin_bytes.py","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil: CRLF and text-mode newline translation on Windows"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","e062-1686-1a27-41a4"],["relates_to","a2da-e61b-989e-4862"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"51c6-9f1d-595b-411f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 11 tests fail on CRLF from core.autocrlf=true or text-mode newline translation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["464d5fe3-771b-43ea-8b2b-296c90afa216","8f893a03-3f14-476c-9f38-029d9a0a60e8","245d8bcf-e220-4f3a-a048-fd36a540c268","99976b82-fa30-4d85-b8e3-9d91b3867987","2c79a18d-99f3-4329-838a-0d59d7f2f78f","ef2ff312-29d9-4abe-b3ca-df313a90be5a","8485a882-4b71-41e8-95bf-0c21ce640405","746d1ab8-d3fa-4c59-8347-c19ecee3ea8a","cf5cf911-0319-42df-9463-f966df7219b3","6e3ff32f-25f5-4380-bc42-2fb7d260746e","03f46e05-ae36-4f41-a39c-2fa33ded1761"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795275206935208002,"uuid":"971fa845-5d54-448a-a4d3-ef2f8778dc26"}